## P18-V01 orderly Push pull follow-up — 2026-10-13

- Audited Java 5.5.1 `DefaultMQPushConsumerImpl.pullMessage` against `PullRequest` and the current Rust pull worker. Found that Java refreshes the configured start offset once when an orderly clustering queue is first locked, then marks the request `previouslyLocked`; Rust carried the matching flag but never read or set it. This could pull from an offset that changed between assignment and the first locked pull.
- Extended the invoked Java 5.5.1 implementation fixture with sequential store offsets (15 then 21). It records that the first locked pull adopts 15, marks `previouslyLocked`, and the next attempt does not reread. Fixture SHA-256: `3407efb21e8c669d49864ff59a2cb3bcbb6382aa45e7a449c6a7ea0cb928869b`.
